# rpmlint's filters for check-linux-packages.sh's run on the RPM packages, each with its reason.
# rpmlint fails a run where a filter matches nothing, so none outlives its reason.

# The command line is the release tarball's, built static against musl so that one binary runs on
# every Linux whatever its C library, as install.sh installs it too. Rust's
# aarch64-unknown-linux-musl target links it at a fixed address, its x86_64 one as static-pie.
addFilter("^pitboard\.\w+: E: (statically-linked-binary|position-independent-executable-suggested) /usr/bin/pitboard$")

# The Plasma widget's package holds the widget's QML and its licence. What the widget does is the
# app's manual page and docs.usepitboard.com's to say, as the Debian package leaves it.
addFilter("^pitboard-plasma-widget\.noarch: E: no-documentation$")
